### API Request Description

This endpoint allows users to log in by providing their email and password.

#### Request Body

- `email` (string) - The email of the user.

- `password` (string) - The password of the user.


#### Response

The response will be in JSON format with the following schema:

``` json
{
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
        "message": {
            "type": "string"
        },
        "status": {
            "type": "boolean"
        },
        "user": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
                "id": {
                    "type": "number"
                },
                "name": {
                    "type": "string"
                },
                "email": {
                    "type": "string"
                },
                "password": {
                    "type": "string"
                },
                "mobile": {
                    "type": "string"
                },
                "role": {
                    "type": "string"
                },
                "otp": {
                    "type": "number"
                },
                "expires_at": {
                    "type": ["string", "null"]
                },
                "is_verified": {
                    "type": "number"
                },
                "status": {
                    "type": "string"
                },
                "city": {
                    "type": "string"
                },
                "state": {
                    "type": "string"
                },
                "address": {
                    "type": "string"
                },
                "aadhar_number": {
                    "type": "string"
                },
                "aadhar_file": {
                    "type": ["string", "null"]
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

 ```

This API endpoint is used to send an OTP to a user's mobile number.

### Request Body

- mobile_number (string, required): The mobile number to which the OTP will be sent.


### Response

The response will be in JSON format with the following properties:

- message (string): A message related to the OTP sending process.

- status (boolean): Indicates the status of the OTP sending process.

- otp (string): The OTP sent to the user's mobile number.


### JSON Schema

``` json
{
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
        "message": {
            "type": "string"
        },
        "status": {
            "type": "boolean"
        },
        "otp": {
            "type": "string"
        }
    }
}

 ```

### Verify OTP for User

This API endpoint is used to verify the OTP (One-Time Password) for a user.

#### Request Body

- `mobile_number` (text): The mobile number for which the OTP is being verified.

- `otp` (text): The One-Time Password to be verified.


#### Response

The response is in JSON format with the following schema:

``` json
{
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
        "message": {
            "type": "string"
        },
        "status": {
            "type": "boolean"
        }
    }
}

 ```

- `message` (string): A message indicating the result of the OTP verification process.

- `status` (boolean): Indicates the status of the OTP verification. `true` for successful verification, `false` for unsuccessful verification.

The `POST /api/users/forgotpassword` endpoint is used to initiate the process of resetting a user's password by sending a one-time password (OTP) to the user's email.

### Request Body

- `email` (text): The email address of the user for whom the password reset process is initiated.


### Response

The response is in JSON format and has the following schema:

``` json
{
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
        "message": {
            "type": "string"
        },
        "status": {
            "type": "boolean"
        },
        "otp": {
            "type": "string"
        }
    }
}

 ```

- `message` (string): A message indicating the result of the password reset initiation process.

- `status` (boolean): Indicates the status of the password reset initiation process.

- `otp` (string): The one-time password (OTP) sent to the user's email for the password reset process.

### Change User Password

This endpoint allows users to change their password.

#### Request Body

- email (text): The email of the user.

- password (text): The new password for the user.


#### Response

The response is in JSON format and has the following schema:

``` json
{
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
        "message": {
            "type": "string"
        },
        "status": {
            "type": "boolean"
        }
    }
}

 ```

### Create New Listing

This endpoint allows the client to submit a new listing.

#### Request Body Parameters

- `project_type` (text) - The type of the project.

- `sale_type` (text) - The type of sale.

- `project_title` (text) - The title of the project.

- `phone` (text) - The phone number associated with the listing.

- `user_id` (text) - The ID of the user submitting the listing.


#### Response

The response is in JSON format and has the following schema:

``` json
{
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
        "message": {
            "type": "string"
        },
        "status": {
            "type": "boolean"
        },
        "listing_id": {
            "type": "integer"
        }
    }
}

 ```

- `message` (string) - A message related to the submission.

- `status` (boolean) - The status of the submission.

- `listing_id` (integer) - The ID of the newly created listing.


